{"availability":"available","full":"apollo-2006/nexus_editor","name":"nexus_editor","description":"Collaborative text editor on a fractional-index CRDT, with a Go WebSocket relay and a three-replica convergence demo.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-23T00:26:56Z","updated":"2026-09-14T01:56:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://apollo-2006.github.io/nexus_editor/","topics":["collaborative-editing","crdt","go","react","typescript","websocket"],"demo":"https://apollo-2006.github.io/nexus_editor/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:58.225Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:58.225Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:58.225Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:58.225Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A real-time collaborative text editor built from scratch. Several people type into the same document at the same time, over a network that delays, reorders and drops them offline, and every copy converges on the same text, with no locking, no operational transform server, and no \"who typed first\" arbitration.","Type into three editors at once in your browser → Three replicas on one page exchange the same JSON operations the Go relay forwards, over a simulated network with adjustable latency and jitter and a per-replica offline switch. A status bar shows when they have converged, and a table shows every character's position."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/apollo-2006/nexus_editor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bd4f44f02f5d8c946c64e481075aa5beb09b013b6c3199c62bb64d9ad3da2193","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:58.388Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:58.388Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A real-time collaborative text editor built from scratch. Several people type into the same document at the same time, over a network that delays, reorders and